\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Let $k$ be a local $p$-adic field and $X/k$ a smooth projective curve of genus at least $2$. Is the natural map from $X(k)$ to conjugacy classes of continuous sections of $$\pi_1(X/k)\longrightarrow\operatorname{Gal}(\overline k/k)$$ a bijection?
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2009/05}{[S2]}.

